From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:35:02 +0300
Subject: Game controllers: a fixed built-in scheme next to the keyboard

Controller N (the N-th opened game controller, N = 1..4) plays player N,
with no binding by hand. The keys keep working at the same time, because
the pads are handled in their own path (Input::padEvent) that drives the
player's actions directly and is never stored in the profile.

  right trigger or R1  accelerate      left trigger or L1  brake
  d-pad left/right, left stick X       flip left / flip right
  A (Cross)                            change direction
  Y (Triangle)                         restart the level
  X (Square)                           restart from the last checkpoint
  Start                                pause (already so)

The table is padBindings in Input.cpp (padGlobalBindings for the restarts),
so swapping buttons is a one-line change. Triggers and the stick are
analog above a dead zone. A pad only changes what it changes, so a held
key is not cancelled by a resting pad; on resume the held pad state is
applied like the held keys. The Options > Controls > Controller tab lists
the scheme as read-only text.

Hot-plug: a pad connected later is opened and takes the first free slot;
an unplugged one frees its slot and releases what it held, the others keep
their player. The restart actions go through Input::isGlobalKey (the bound
key or the pad button).

Controller events are always on, so the pad works whatever "Enable
joysticks" says (a saved false included); the option now defaults to true
and is only remembered. Menus keep what X-Moto had: d-pad, left stick, A
and B.

